From: LuminolLeaf <noreply@luminolleaf.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix dragon still healing after death

When the dragon is dealt its killing blow outside of the sitting phase,
handleKillingBlow() does not kill it outright; instead it sets the health
to 1 and switches to the DYING phase while the death animation plays.
During that window isDeadOrDying() still returns false (health > 0), so
aiStep() keeps calling checkCrystals(). If an end crystal is nearby the
dragon is then healed throughout its own death animation, which can stall
or break the death sequence. Avoid healing while the dragon is in the
DYING phase.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/boss/enderdragon/EnderDragon.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/boss/enderdragon/EnderDragon.java
index 00000000000000000000000000000000000000000..00000000000000000000000000000000000000001 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/boss/enderdragon/EnderDragon.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/boss/enderdragon/EnderDragon.java
@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@ public class EnderDragon extends Mob implements Enemy {
             if (this.nearestCrystal.isRemoved()) {
                 this.nearestCrystal = null;
-            } else if (this.tickCount % 10 == 0 && this.getHealth() < this.getMaxHealth()) {
+            } else if (this.tickCount % 10 == 0 && this.getHealth() < this.getMaxHealth() && this.phaseManager.getCurrentPhase().getPhase() != EnderDragonPhase.DYING) { // LuminolLeaf - Fix dragon still healing after death
                 this.setHealth(this.getHealth() + 1.0F);
             }
         }
